Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was a memory leak in the `mwifiex_tm_cmd` function due to the `hostcmd` structure being allocated with `kzalloc` but not being freed in all error handling paths. Specifically, if the function encountered an error after allocating `hostcmd`, it would exit without freeing the allocated memory, leading to a memory leak. The patch added necessary `kfree(hostcmd)` calls to ensure that the allocated memory is properly released before returning from the function in case of errors.
